    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Feature engineering: seasonality\n",
        "The dataset includes monthly availability columns for both hemispheres:\n",
        "- NH = Northern Hemisphere\n",
        "- SH = Southern Hemisphere\n",
        "\n",
        "Missing values in these monthly columns typically indicate that an insect is not available during that month in the corresponding hemisphere.\n",
        "\n",
        "To simplify the dataset, I decided to represent seasonal availability using numeric features instead of individual monthly columns:\n",
        "- \"Months_Available_NH\": number of months the insect is available in the Northern Hemisphere\n",
        "- \"Months_Available_SH\": number of months the insect is available in the Southern Hemisphere"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "z7FY0t7pu6rS"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "nh_month_cols = [c for c in data.columns if c.startswith(\"NH \")]\n",
        "sh_month_cols = [c for c in data.columns if c.startswith(\"SH \")]\n",
        "\n",
        "data[\"Months_Available_NH\"] = data[nh_month_cols].notna().sum(axis=1)\n",
        "data[\"Months_Available_SH\"] = data[sh_month_cols].notna().sum(axis=1)\n",
        "data[[\"Months_Available_NH\", \"Months_Available_SH\"]].head()"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 206
        },
